2003..2077 Comment "/// Reading twice is reading once at the same state. The inner `get` is an"
2078..2148 Comment "/// instance of the rule\'s own left side through its pattern, and both"
2149..2220 Comment "/// reducts read once and continue at that state three times (#2116). A"
2221..2298 Comment "/// scope over this theory runs its subject normalised by the rule: `run a <-"
2299..2375 Comment "/// st.get(); run b <- st.get(); pure a + b` reads once, `run a <- st.get();"
2376..2449 Comment "/// pure a + a` with `b` bound to `a` (`state-laws.gandr`\'s `readTwice`)."
